function Get-WsmLabCheck([string]$Code,[string]$Status,[string]$ItemId='',[string]$Adapter='',[string]$Field='',[string]$ExpectedHash='',[string]$ObservedHash='',[string]$Hint='',[string]$FailureCategory='',$NativeCode=$null,[string]$HResult='') {
    [pscustomobject][ordered]@{Code=$Code;Status=$Status;ItemId=$ItemId;Adapter=$Adapter;Field=$Field;ExpectedSHA256=$ExpectedHash;ObservedSHA256=$ObservedHash;FailureCategory=$FailureCategory;NativeCode=$NativeCode;HResult=$HResult;Hint=$Hint}
}
function Get-WsmLabSafeFailure($Failure) {
    try{$details=Get-WsmFailureDetails $Failure;[pscustomobject]@{Category=[string]$details.Category;NativeCode=$details.NativeCode;HResult=[string]$details.HResult}}
    catch{[pscustomobject]@{Category='OperationFailure';NativeCode=$null;HResult=''}}
}
function Test-WsmLabPathOverlap([string]$Candidate,[string[]]$Scopes) {
    $path=(Get-WsmPhysicalPath $Candidate).TrimEnd('\');foreach($scopeValue in $Scopes){if([string]::IsNullOrWhiteSpace($scopeValue)){continue};$scope=(Get-WsmPhysicalPath $scopeValue).TrimEnd('\');if($path -ieq $scope -or $path.StartsWith($scope+'\',[StringComparison]::OrdinalIgnoreCase) -or $scope.StartsWith($path+'\',[StringComparison]::OrdinalIgnoreCase)){return $true}};$false
}
function Test-WsmLabFileScopeCheck($Item,$Package,[string]$Root) {
    $itemId=[string]$Item.ItemId;$adapter='FileScope'
    try{$result=Test-WsmFileScope $Item $Package $Root;if($result.Passed){Get-WsmLabCheck 'FileScopeExact' 'PASS' $itemId $adapter 'FileScopeContentAndMetadata' '' ([string]$result.ActualHash) 'Every selected file matched its approved artifact content and metadata.'}else{Get-WsmLabCheck 'FileScopeExact' 'FAIL' $itemId $adapter 'FileScopeContentAndMetadata' '' ([string]$result.ActualHash) 'Approved scope differs or is incomplete.'}}
    catch{$failure=Get-WsmLabSafeFailure $_;Get-WsmLabCheck 'FileScopeReadable' 'Blocked' $itemId $adapter 'ApprovedScope' '' '' 'Scope could not be safely read; inspect the host locally.' $failure.Category $failure.NativeCode $failure.HResult}
}
function Assert-WsmLabStateBinding($Manifest,[string]$ManifestHash,[string]$StateDirectory) {
    if(-not [IO.Directory]::Exists($StateDirectory)){throw (New-WsmContractError 'Target operation state directory is absent.')}
    $pairRoot=Join-Path ([IO.Path]::GetFullPath($StateDirectory)) ([string]$Manifest.PairId);Assert-WsmNoReparse $pairRoot
    $statePath=Join-Path $pairRoot 'state.json';$journalPath=Join-Path $pairRoot 'journal.jsonl'
    if(-not [IO.File]::Exists($statePath) -or -not [IO.File]::Exists($journalPath)){throw (New-WsmContractError 'Target operation state or journal is absent.')}
    Assert-WsmNoReparse $statePath;Assert-WsmNoReparse $journalPath;$state=Read-WsmJson $statePath;Assert-WsmEnvelope $state 'OperationState'
    if($state.PairId -cne $Manifest.PairId -or $state.TargetFingerprint -cne $Manifest.Target.Fingerprint -or $state.PlanHash -ine $Manifest.PlanHash -or $state.ManifestHash -ine $ManifestHash -or $state.Generation -ne $Manifest.Generation){throw (New-WsmContractError 'Target operation state is foreign or bound to another package generation.')}
    $journal=Test-WsmJournal $StateDirectory $Manifest.PairId;if(-not $journal.Consistent){throw (New-WsmContractError 'Target operation journal is inconsistent.')}
    [pscustomobject]@{State=$state;Journal=$journal;Root=$pairRoot}
}
function Assert-WsmLabEnvironmentConfirmationReferences {
    [CmdletBinding()]
    param([Parameter(Mandatory)][object[]]$References,[Parameter(Mandatory)]$Manifest)
    if($References.Count -gt 20){throw (New-WsmContractError 'At most 20 environment confirmation references may be attached.')}
    $safe=New-Object 'System.Collections.Generic.List[object]'
    foreach($reference in $References){
        Assert-WsmFields $reference @('Path','SHA256') @('Path','SHA256')
        $path=[string]$reference.Path;$hash=[string]$reference.SHA256
        if([string]::IsNullOrWhiteSpace($path) -or $hash -notmatch '^[a-fA-F0-9]{64}$'){throw (New-WsmContractError 'Environment confirmation reference requires a path and independent SHA256.')}
        $fullPath=[IO.Path]::GetFullPath($path);Assert-WsmNoReparse $fullPath
        if(-not [IO.File]::Exists($fullPath) -or (Get-Item -LiteralPath $fullPath).Length -gt 128MB){throw (New-WsmContractError 'Environment confirmation JSON is missing or exceeds the 128 MiB limit.')}
        $document=Read-WsmTrustedJson $fullPath $hash
        Assert-WsmFields $document @('SchemaVersion','ToolVersion','Kind','DocumentId','PairId','InventoryRevision','DecisionRevision','TargetObservationRevision','SourceInventoryProjectionHash','ReportProjectionHash','GeneratedUtc','Projection','Counts','Status','AuthoritativeDecisionInput','ProductionQualified') @('SchemaVersion','ToolVersion','Kind','DocumentId','PairId','InventoryRevision','DecisionRevision','TargetObservationRevision','SourceInventoryProjectionHash','ReportProjectionHash','GeneratedUtc','Projection','Counts','Status','AuthoritativeDecisionInput','ProductionQualified')
        Assert-WsmEnvelope $document 'EnvironmentConfirmation'
        $projection=$document.Projection
        Assert-WsmFields $projection @('SchemaVersion','Kind','PairId','Source','CaptureContext','SourceInventoryProjectionHash','InventoryRevision','InventoryHash','DecisionRevision','ToolVersion','Phase','PlanHash','GeneratedUtc','TargetObservation','TargetDiff','Coverage','Software','PreparationRequirements','RuntimeEvidence','OracleConfiguration','WindowsDecisions','Items','SpecialProducts','Unknowns','Requirements','ReadinessProjection','EvidenceReceipts','Blockers','OwnerHandoff','Counts','ProductionQualified','TrustStatement') @('SchemaVersion','Kind','PairId','Source','SourceInventoryProjectionHash','InventoryRevision','InventoryHash','DecisionRevision','ToolVersion','Phase','PlanHash','GeneratedUtc','Counts','ProductionQualified')
        Assert-WsmFields $projection.Source @('HostId','Fingerprint','Name','OS','Build','Edition','InstallationType','Architecture') @('HostId','Fingerprint')
        $documentGuid=[Guid]::Empty
        if(-not [Guid]::TryParse([string]$document.DocumentId,[ref]$documentGuid) -or $documentGuid.ToString('D') -cne ([string]$document.DocumentId).ToLowerInvariant()){throw (New-WsmContractError 'Environment confirmation DocumentId is invalid.')}
        foreach($field in @('SourceInventoryProjectionHash','ReportProjectionHash')){if([string]$document.$field -notmatch '^[a-fA-F0-9]{64}$'){throw (New-WsmContractError ('Environment confirmation '+$field+' is invalid.'))}}
        if($document.AuthoritativeDecisionInput -isnot [bool] -or $document.AuthoritativeDecisionInput -or $document.ProductionQualified -isnot [bool] -or $document.ProductionQualified -or $document.Status -cne 'Generated'){throw (New-WsmContractError 'Environment confirmation is not a report-only generated document.')}
        if($document.PairId -cne $Manifest.PairId -or $projection.PairId -cne $Manifest.PairId -or $projection.Source.Fingerprint -cne $Manifest.Source.Fingerprint -or $projection.PlanHash -cne $Manifest.PlanHash -or $projection.InventoryRevision -ne $Manifest.InventoryRevision -or $projection.DecisionRevision -ne $Manifest.DecisionRevision -or $document.ToolVersion -cne $projection.ToolVersion -or $document.GeneratedUtc -cne $projection.GeneratedUtc){throw (New-WsmContractError 'Environment confirmation belongs to another pair, source, plan, revision, or projection time.')}
        if($document.InventoryRevision -ne $Manifest.InventoryRevision -or $document.DecisionRevision -ne $Manifest.DecisionRevision -or $document.TargetObservationRevision -isnot [long] -and $document.TargetObservationRevision -isnot [int]){throw (New-WsmContractError 'Environment confirmation top-level revisions are invalid or stale.')}
        if($document.SourceInventoryProjectionHash -ine $projection.SourceInventoryProjectionHash){throw (New-WsmContractError 'Environment confirmation source projection binding is inconsistent.')}
        if((ConvertTo-Json -InputObject $document.Counts -Depth 12 -Compress) -cne (ConvertTo-Json -InputObject $projection.Counts -Depth 12 -Compress)){throw (New-WsmContractError 'Environment confirmation top-level counts differ from the hashed projection.')}
        $projectionJson=ConvertTo-Json -InputObject $projection -Depth 45 -Compress;$projectionHash=Get-WsmHashText $projectionJson
        if($projectionHash -ine [string]$document.ReportProjectionHash){throw (New-WsmContractError 'Environment confirmation report projection hash does not match its content.')}
        if($projection.ProductionQualified -isnot [bool] -or $projection.ProductionQualified){throw (New-WsmContractError 'Environment confirmation projection claims unsupported qualification.')}
        $safe.Add([pscustomobject][ordered]@{DocumentId=[string]$document.DocumentId;PairId=[string]$document.PairId;Path=$fullPath;SHA256=$hash.ToLowerInvariant();SourceInventoryProjectionHash=[string]$document.SourceInventoryProjectionHash.ToLowerInvariant();ReportProjectionHash=[string]$document.ReportProjectionHash.ToLowerInvariant();InventoryRevision=[long]$document.InventoryRevision;DecisionRevision=[long]$document.DecisionRevision;TargetObservationRevision=[long]$document.TargetObservationRevision;GeneratedUtc=[string]$document.GeneratedUtc;Status='ReportOnly';AuthoritativeDecisionInput=$false;ReadinessProof=$false})
    }
    $safe.ToArray()
}
function Assert-WsmLabDeliveryReceiptReferences {
    [CmdletBinding()]
    param([Parameter(Mandatory)][object[]]$References,[Parameter(Mandatory)]$Manifest,[Parameter(Mandatory)]$Plan,[Parameter(Mandatory)][string]$ManifestHash,[Parameter(Mandatory)][string]$ToolFingerprint)
    if($References.Count -gt 20){throw (New-WsmContractError 'At most 20 delivery receipt references may be attached.')}
    $safe=New-Object 'System.Collections.Generic.List[object]';$seen=@{}
    foreach($reference in $References){
        Assert-WsmFields $reference @('Path','SHA256') @('Path','SHA256')
        $path=[string]$reference.Path;$hash=[string]$reference.SHA256
        if([string]::IsNullOrWhiteSpace($path) -or $hash -notmatch '^[a-fA-F0-9]{64}$'){throw (New-WsmContractError 'Delivery receipt reference requires a path and independent SHA256.')}
        $fullPath=[IO.Path]::GetFullPath($path);Assert-WsmNoReparse $fullPath
        if(-not [IO.File]::Exists($fullPath) -or (Get-Item -LiteralPath $fullPath).Length -gt 128MB){throw (New-WsmContractError 'Delivery receipt JSON is missing or exceeds the 128 MiB limit.')}
        $receipt=Read-WsmTrustedJson $fullPath $hash;Assert-WsmEnvelope $receipt 'DeliveryReceipt'
        if($receipt.Status -cnotin @('Sealed','ImportedVerified') -or $receipt.OperationKind -cnotin @('Full','Delta')){throw (New-WsmContractError 'Delivery receipt status or operation kind is unsupported.')}
        $baseHash='';$baseStatus='None'
        if($receipt.OperationKind -ceq 'Delta'){$baseHash=[string]$Manifest.BaseManifestHash;$baseStatus='VerifiedTrustedBase';if(-not $baseHash -or $receipt.BaseManifestHash -ine $baseHash){throw (New-WsmContractError 'Delta delivery receipt does not bind the current package base manifest.')}}
        elseif($Manifest.BaseManifestHash){$baseHash=[string]$Manifest.BaseManifestHash;$baseStatus=[string]$receipt.BaseVerificationStatus;if($baseStatus -notin @('ReferenceOnly','VerifiedTrustedBase') -or $receipt.BaseManifestHash -ine $baseHash){throw (New-WsmContractError 'Full delivery receipt base reference differs from the current manifest.')}}
        elseif($receipt.BaseVerificationStatus -cne 'None' -or $receipt.BaseManifestHash){throw (New-WsmContractError 'Full delivery receipt contains an unexpected base binding.')}
        [void](Assert-WsmDeliveryReceipt -Path $fullPath -ExpectedHash $hash -PairId ([string]$Manifest.PairId) -PlanHash ([string]$Manifest.PlanHash) -SourceHostId ([string]$Manifest.Source.HostId) -SourceFingerprint ([string]$Manifest.Source.Fingerprint) -TargetHostId ([string]$Manifest.Target.HostId) -TargetFingerprint ([string]$Manifest.Target.Fingerprint) -ToolFingerprint $ToolFingerprint -ApprovalId ([string]$Plan.ApprovalId) -Generation ([int]$Manifest.Generation) -ManifestHash $ManifestHash -OperationKind ([string]$receipt.OperationKind) -BaseVerificationStatus $baseStatus -BaseManifestHash $baseHash -ExpectedStatus ([string]$receipt.Status))
        if($receipt.PackageId -cne $Manifest.PackageId -or $receipt.BatchId -cne $Manifest.BatchId -or $receipt.ToolFingerprint -ine $Plan.ToolFingerprint){throw (New-WsmContractError 'Delivery receipt package, batch, or approved tool binding differs.')}
        if($seen.ContainsKey([string]$receipt.ReceiptId)){throw (New-WsmContractError 'Duplicate delivery ReceiptId reference.')};$seen[[string]$receipt.ReceiptId]=$true
        $safe.Add([pscustomobject][ordered]@{ReceiptId=[string]$receipt.ReceiptId;DeliveryId=[string]$receipt.DeliveryId;Status=[string]$receipt.Status;Mode=[string]$receipt.Mode;OperationKind=[string]$receipt.OperationKind;BaseVerificationStatus=[string]$receipt.BaseVerificationStatus;PairId=[string]$receipt.PairId;PlanHash=([string]$receipt.PlanHash).ToLowerInvariant();Generation=[long]$receipt.Generation;PackageId=[string]$receipt.PackageId;ManifestHash=([string]$receipt.ManifestHash).ToLowerInvariant();BaseManifestHash=([string]$receipt.BaseManifestHash).ToLowerInvariant();TransportHash=([string]$receipt.TransportHash).ToLowerInvariant();Path=$fullPath;SHA256=$hash.ToLowerInvariant();ReportOnly=$true;ReadinessProof=$false;ProductionVerified=$false})
    }
    $safe.ToArray()
}
function Export-WsmLabValidationReport {
    [CmdletBinding()]
    param(
        [Parameter(Mandatory)][string]$OutputDirectory,
        [Parameter(Mandatory)][ValidateSet('Source','Target')][string]$Role,
        [string]$ManifestPath,
        [string]$ExpectedHash,
        [string]$StateDirectory,
        [ValidateSet('Staged','Final')][string]$Phase='Staged',
        [object[]]$GeneralHostEvidence=@(),
        [object[]]$EnvironmentConfirmationReferences=@(),
        [object[]]$DeliveryReceiptReferences=@(),
        [ValidateRange(1,1000)][int]$TextCheckLimit=200
    )
    $operationLock=$null
    try {
    if([bool]$ManifestPath -ne [bool]$ExpectedHash){throw (New-WsmContractError 'ManifestPath and ExpectedHash must be supplied together.')}
    if($Role -eq 'Target' -and $ManifestPath -and -not $StateDirectory){throw (New-WsmContractError 'Target lab verification with a package requires its approved operation state directory.')}
    if($ExpectedHash -and $ExpectedHash -notmatch '^[A-Fa-f0-9]{64}$'){throw (New-WsmContractError 'ExpectedHash must be a SHA256 value.')}
    $languageMode=[string]$ExecutionContext.SessionState.LanguageMode
    if($languageMode -ceq 'FullLanguage'){$identity=Get-WsmMachineIdentity}else{$preflight=Get-WsmPreflight;$identity=[pscustomobject]@{Fingerprint='';Name='';OS=$preflight.OS;Version=$preflight.Version;IsServer=[bool]$preflight.IsServer;Administrator=[bool]$preflight.Administrator;Is64Bit=[bool]$preflight.Is64Bit}}
    Assert-WsmFields $identity @('Fingerprint','Name','OS','Version','IsServer','Administrator','Is64Bit') @('Fingerprint','OS','Version','IsServer','Administrator','Is64Bit');if(($identity.Fingerprint -and ($identity.Fingerprint -isnot [string] -or $identity.Fingerprint -notmatch '^[a-fA-F0-9]{64}$')) -or $identity.IsServer -isnot [bool] -or $identity.Administrator -isnot [bool] -or $identity.Is64Bit -isnot [bool]){throw (New-WsmContractError 'Host identity has an invalid environment shape.')};if($ManifestPath -and -not $identity.Fingerprint){throw (New-WsmContractError 'Trusted package verification requires FullLanguage machine identity checks.')};$toolFingerprint=Get-WsmToolFingerprint;if($toolFingerprint -isnot [string] -or $toolFingerprint -notmatch '^[a-fA-F0-9]{64}$'){throw (New-WsmContractError 'Installed tool fingerprint is invalid.')}
    $installationType='Unknown'
    try{$installationType=[string](Get-ItemProperty -LiteralPath 'HKLM:\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows NT\CurrentVersion' -Name InstallationType -ErrorAction Stop).InstallationType}catch{}
    $uiCulture=[Globalization.CultureInfo]::CurrentUICulture.Name;$culture=[Globalization.CultureInfo]::CurrentCulture.Name
    $psEdition='Desktop';if($PSVersionTable.ContainsKey('PSEdition')){$psEdition=[string]$PSVersionTable.PSEdition}
    $manifest=$null;$package=$null;$stateBinding=$null
    if($ManifestPath){
        # Read package and identity bindings before creating any output, so wrong-host or tampered inputs leave no report artifact.
        $package=Test-WsmMigrationPackage $ManifestPath $ExpectedHash;$manifest=$package.Manifest
        $expectedFingerprint=[string]$manifest.Source.Fingerprint;if($Role -eq 'Target'){$expectedFingerprint=[string]$manifest.Target.Fingerprint}
        if($identity.Fingerprint -cne $expectedFingerprint){throw (New-WsmContractError 'This host does not match the approved package role fingerprint.')}
        if($package.Plan.ToolFingerprint -ine $toolFingerprint){throw (New-WsmContractError 'Installed tool fingerprint differs from approved plan tool fingerprint.')}
        if($Role -eq 'Target'){
            $pairRoot=Join-Path ([IO.Path]::GetFullPath($StateDirectory)) $manifest.PairId;Assert-WsmNoReparse $pairRoot
            $lockPath=Join-Path $pairRoot '.wsm.lock';Assert-WsmNoReparse $lockPath
            if(-not [IO.File]::Exists($lockPath)){throw (New-WsmContractError 'Target operation lock is absent; no completed restore checkpoint can be adopted.')}
            try{$operationLock=[IO.File]::Open($lockPath,'Open','Read','None')}catch{throw (New-WsmContractError 'Target operation is busy or its lock cannot be read; retry the report after the local operation finishes.')}
            $stateBinding=Assert-WsmLabStateBinding $manifest $ExpectedHash $StateDirectory
        }
    }
    $safeEnvironmentConfirmationReferences=@()
    if($EnvironmentConfirmationReferences.Count){if(-not $manifest){throw (New-WsmContractError 'Environment confirmation references require a trusted migration package binding.')};$safeEnvironmentConfirmationReferences=@(Assert-WsmLabEnvironmentConfirmationReferences -References $EnvironmentConfirmationReferences -Manifest $manifest)}
    $safeDeliveryReceiptReferences=@()
    if($DeliveryReceiptReferences.Count){if(-not $manifest){throw (New-WsmContractError 'Delivery receipt references require a trusted migration package binding.')};$safeDeliveryReceiptReferences=@(Assert-WsmLabDeliveryReceiptReferences -References $DeliveryReceiptReferences -Manifest $manifest -Plan $package.Plan -ManifestHash $ExpectedHash -ToolFingerprint $toolFingerprint)}
    $included=@();$scopeRoots=New-Object 'System.Collections.Generic.List[string]'
    if($manifest){$included=@($package.Plan.Items | Where-Object Decision -CEQ Include);foreach($item in $included){if($item.MigrationSpec.Adapter -eq 'FileScope'){$scopeRoots.Add([string]$item.MigrationSpec.SourcePath);$scopeRoots.Add([string]$item.MigrationSpec.TargetPath)}}}
    $protectedPaths=@($scopeRoots.ToArray());if($StateDirectory){$protectedPaths+=@($StateDirectory)}
    $outputRoot=[IO.Path]::GetFullPath($OutputDirectory);Assert-WsmNoReparse $outputRoot;if(Test-WsmLabPathOverlap $outputRoot $protectedPaths){throw (New-WsmContractError 'Report output overlaps an approved file scope or operation state directory.')};if(-not [IO.Directory]::Exists($outputRoot)){[void][IO.Directory]::CreateDirectory($outputRoot)}
    $runRoot=Join-Path $outputRoot ('lab-validation-'+[Guid]::NewGuid().ToString('N'));[void][IO.Directory]::CreateDirectory($runRoot);Protect-WsmDirectory $runRoot
    $checks=New-Object 'System.Collections.Generic.List[object]'
    $osDescription=[string]$identity.OS;$osVersion=[string]$identity.Version
    $checks.Add((Get-WsmLabCheck 'HostIsServer' $(if($identity.IsServer){'PASS'}else{'FAIL'}) '' '' 'WindowsServer' '' '' 'Host operating system role.'))
    $checks.Add((Get-WsmLabCheck 'Administrator' $(if($identity.Administrator){'PASS'}else{'FAIL'}) '' '' 'ElevatedAdministrator' '' '' 'Current token elevation.'))
    $checks.Add((Get-WsmLabCheck 'ProcessArchitecture' $(if($identity.Is64Bit){'PASS'}else{'FAIL'}) '' '' '64Bit' '' '' 'PowerShell process architecture.'))
    $checks.Add((Get-WsmLabCheck 'LanguageMode' $(if($languageMode -ceq 'FullLanguage'){'PASS'}else{'FAIL'}) '' '' 'FullLanguage' '' '' 'PowerShell language mode.'))
    $checks.Add((Get-WsmLabCheck 'InstalledToolFingerprint' 'PASS' '' '' 'ToolBytes' $toolFingerprint $toolFingerprint 'Fingerprint of locally installed migration tool files.'))
    $environmentCapabilities=New-Object 'System.Collections.Generic.List[object]'
    if($manifest){foreach($item in $included){$adapter=[string]$item.MigrationSpec.Adapter;$commands=@(Get-WsmAdapterRequiredCommands $adapter);if($adapter -eq 'FileScope'){$commands=@()};if($adapter -eq 'ManualWorkflow'){$commands=@()};foreach($command in $commands){if($environmentCapabilities -notcontains $command){$environmentCapabilities.Add($command)}}}}
    foreach($command in $environmentCapabilities){$available=$null -ne (Get-Command $command -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue);$checks.Add((Get-WsmLabCheck 'AdapterCommand' $(if($available){'PASS'}else{'FAIL'}) '' '' ([string]$command) '' '' $(if($available){'Required local command is available.'}else{'Required local command is unavailable.'})))}
    if(-not $manifest){$checks.Add((Get-WsmLabCheck 'ApprovedPackage' 'NotTested' '' '' 'ExactPackageBinding' '' '' 'No independently trusted package was supplied; this is environment readiness only.'))}
    else {
        $checks.Add((Get-WsmLabCheck 'ApprovedPackage' 'PASS' '' '' 'ManifestAndPlan' ([string]$ExpectedHash) ([string]$package.SHA256) 'Package, plan, artifact index and payload hashes validated.'))
        $checks.Add((Get-WsmLabCheck 'RoleFingerprint' 'PASS' '' '' $Role $expectedFingerprint ([string]$identity.Fingerprint) 'Machine identity matches the exact approved source or target binding.'))
        if($Role -eq 'Source'){
            $collectorRoot=Join-Path $runRoot 'collector';[void][IO.Directory]::CreateDirectory($collectorRoot);Protect-WsmDirectory $collectorRoot
            try {
                $inventoryResult=Export-WsmInventory -OutputDirectory $collectorRoot -DeepDiscovery:($package.Plan.Source.PSObject.Properties['DiscoveryDepth'] -and $package.Plan.Source.DiscoveryDepth -ceq 'Deep')
                $inventory=Read-WsmTrustedJson $inventoryResult.Path $inventoryResult.SHA256
                if($inventory.Source.Fingerprint -cne $manifest.Source.Fingerprint){throw 'Collector source binding differs.'}
                $checks.Add((Get-WsmLabCheck 'NativeInventoryCollected' 'PASS' '' '' 'CollectorSnapshot' '' ([string]$inventoryResult.SHA256) 'Read-only native collector snapshot is retained in the protected report directory.'))
                foreach($item in $included){if($item.PSObject.Properties['Kind'] -and $item.Kind -ceq 'ManualItem'){$checks.Add((Get-WsmLabCheck 'SourceInventoryBinding' 'NotTested' ([string]$item.ItemId) ([string]$item.MigrationSpec.Adapter) 'ManualInventoryItem' '' '' 'Owner-added manual inventory item requires separate evidence.'));$checks.Add((Get-WsmLabCheck 'BusinessEvidence' 'NotTested' ([string]$item.ItemId) ([string]$item.MigrationSpec.Adapter) 'OwnerBusinessChecks' '' '' 'Manual business procedure remains unverified.'));continue};$matches=@($inventory.Items | Where-Object ItemId -CEQ $item.ItemId);$status='PASS';$observed='';$hint='Native collector item identity and exact settings fingerprint matched the approved inventory.';if($matches.Count -ne 1){$status='FAIL';$hint='Native inventory item is missing or ambiguous.'}else{$observed=[string]$matches[0].SettingsHash;if($observed -ine [string]$item.SettingsHash){$status='FAIL';$hint='Native settings fingerprint differs from approved inventory.'};if($matches[0].Status -ne 'Success'){$status='FAIL';$hint='Native collector did not complete this item.'}};$checks.Add((Get-WsmLabCheck 'SourceInventoryBinding' $status ([string]$item.ItemId) ([string]$item.MigrationSpec.Adapter) 'SettingsHash' ([string]$item.SettingsHash) $observed $hint))
                    if($item.MigrationSpec.Adapter -eq 'FileScope'){$scopeResult=Test-WsmLabFileScopeCheck $item $package ([string]$item.MigrationSpec.SourcePath);$checks.Add($scopeResult)}elseif($item.MigrationSpec.Adapter -eq 'ManualWorkflow'){$checks.Add((Get-WsmLabCheck 'ManualWorkflow' 'NotTested' ([string]$item.ItemId) 'ManualWorkflow' 'BusinessProcedure' '' '' 'Manual procedure requires owner execution and separate business evidence.'))};$businessCount=0;if($item.MigrationSpec.PSObject.Properties['BusinessChecks']){$businessCount=@($item.MigrationSpec.BusinessChecks).Count};$checks.Add((Get-WsmLabCheck 'BusinessEvidence' 'NotTested' ([string]$item.ItemId) ([string]$item.MigrationSpec.Adapter) 'OwnerBusinessChecks' '' '' ('Business acceptance remains unsatisfied; checks recorded: '+$businessCount+'.')))
                }
            } catch {
                $failure=Get-WsmLabSafeFailure $_;$checks.Add((Get-WsmLabCheck 'NativeInventoryCollected' 'Blocked' '' '' 'CollectorSnapshot' '' '' 'Native collector could not complete safely; inspect the protected local output and rerun.' $failure.Category $failure.NativeCode $failure.HResult))
                foreach($item in $included){
                    if($item.MigrationSpec.Adapter -eq 'ManualWorkflow'){$checks.Add((Get-WsmLabCheck 'ManualWorkflow' 'NotTested' ([string]$item.ItemId) 'ManualWorkflow' 'BusinessProcedure' '' '' 'Manual procedure requires owner execution and separate business evidence.'))}
                    elseif($item.MigrationSpec.Adapter -eq 'FileScope'){$checks.Add((Get-WsmLabCheck 'FileScopeExact' 'NotTested' ([string]$item.ItemId) 'FileScope' 'FileScopeContentAndMetadata' '' '' 'Source collector did not complete.'))}
                    $checks.Add((Get-WsmLabCheck 'BusinessEvidence' 'NotTested' ([string]$item.ItemId) ([string]$item.MigrationSpec.Adapter) 'OwnerBusinessChecks' '' '' 'Business acceptance remains unsatisfied by this technical report.'))
                }
            }
        } else {
            $state=$stateBinding.State;$checks.Add((Get-WsmLabCheck 'OperationStateBinding' 'PASS' '' '' 'PairPlanManifestGeneration' ([string]$ExpectedHash) ([string]$state.ManifestHash) 'State and durable journal match the exact package generation and target.'))
            $checks.Add((Get-WsmLabCheck 'JournalConsistency' 'PASS' '' '' 'SequenceAndHashChain' ([string]$state.JournalHash) ([string]$stateBinding.Journal.JournalHash) 'Journal chain matches the state checkpoint.'))
            $validStages=@('Succeeded','ManualEvidenceRequired','RebootRequired');if($Phase -eq 'Final'){$validStages+=@('PostCutoverValidationRequired')};$stageStatus='PASS';if($state.Stage -notin $validStages -or @($state.PendingOperations).Count){$stageStatus='Blocked'};$checks.Add((Get-WsmLabCheck 'OperationStateStage' $stageStatus '' '' $Phase '' '' $(if($stageStatus -eq 'PASS'){'Operation is at a completed checkpoint for this phase.'}else{'Operation is incomplete, failed, cancelled, or has pending work; reconcile before treating readback as complete.'})))
            if($Phase -ceq 'Final'){$activationStatus='Blocked';if($state.Cutover -and $state.Cutover.Stage -ceq 'Activated' -and $state.Stage -ceq 'PostCutoverValidationRequired'){$activationStatus='PASS'};$checks.Add((Get-WsmLabCheck 'FinalActivation' $activationStatus '' '' 'CompletedActivationCheckpoint' '' '' 'Final phase requires the durable completed activation checkpoint.'))}
